{"id": "Dfclb6lRFB_", "title": "Video by therishikatha", "description": "How do you do Lakshmi Puja at home, step by step? 🪔 Here's the whole Diwali puja vidhi in 14 steps. SAVE it for tomorrow evening.\n\nLakshmi Puja is on Sunday, 8 November, after sunset in Pradosh Kaal (Delhi: about 5:54–7:50 PM; check your city's muhurat).\n\n1. Clean everything. Metal murtis get a bath; clay murtis just a gentle wipe.\n2. A red cloth on a clean chowki.\n3. Place the murtis. Many homes, as you face them: Saraswati, Lakshmi, Ganesha.\n4. New clothes, a mala, flowers, and a lotus for Lakshmi.\n5. The kalash: water, a coin, supari and rice inside; five mango leaves, a coconut in red cloth, a kumkum swastik, red mauli round its neck.\n6. Sit facing east or north. Achaman: sip water three times.\n7. Sankalp: water, rice and a flower in your hand. Say your name, the day, and why you pray.\n8. Always begin with Ganesha. In the Shiva Purana (Rudra Samhita, Kumara Khanda 18) the gods made him the first to be worshipped.\n9. Each god in turn: tilak, akshat, flowers, incense, a lamp and bhog, with their mantra.\n Om Gam Ganapataye Namah · Om Shreem Mahalakshmyai Namah · Om Aim Saraswatyai Namah\n10. Havan, if your family does one.\n11. Aarti: Ganesha first, then Lakshmi.\n12. Pushpanjali: flowers in folded hands.\n13. Ask forgiveness for any mistake: \"Mantra-heenam kriya-heenam bhakti-heenam Sureshwara, yat poojitam maya Deva paripoornam tadastu me.\"\n14. Light diyas in every room, rangoli and Lakshmi's footprints at the door. Many homes keep one lamp burning all night.\n\nEvery family does it a little differently, and that's the beauty of it. 🙏\n\nWant your kids to know the stories behind our gods? The Navadurga Set of picture books is out now. Link in bio · rishikatha.com\n\n💬 Who sits where on YOUR chowki? Comment your order!\n🔖 Save this for tomorrow and send it to the one who does the puja at home.\n\n#lakshmipuja #diwali2026 #diwalipuja #pujavidhi #lakshmiganesh #deepavali #diwali #hindutraditions #sanatandharma #mandir #kalash #aarti #hinduculture #rishikatha #indianfestivals", "channel": "therishikatha", "uploader_id": "22569163881", "uploader": "Rishi Katha", "timestamp": 1794068126, "like_count": 9001, "comment_count": 19, "http_headers": {"Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-1483891280220710a", "ext": "m4a", "tbr": 53.851, "asr": 48000, "format_note": "DASH audio", "container": "m4a_dash", "vcodec": "none", "acodec": "mp4a.40.5", "url": "https://instagram.fblr2-2.fna.fbcdn.net/o1/v/t2/f2/m78/AQPg35HTK-fu5jmx-vX0lko43OAUjCCsTNt0bK0UMnh-slQXfBeI_3EZC1O9iz2DqFQtmoB3gVvKLmyRABIcKfrYRwJjhAcDcdSQkuo.mp4?_nc_cat=101&_nc_oc=Ado4Bt8M9UEpQutXd7GmTTnzKq0EbGV6AIQbkifZqN1iJymgSFGJeDmmroF2agjmcL09l54f5AOuVwLUirC8f1T3&_nc_sid=9ca052&_nc_ht=instagram.fblr2-2.fna.fbcdn.net&_nc_ohc=tWv1SjLGqboQ7kNvwGgYfMW&%3D%3D&ccb=17-1&_nc_gid=Qtr95atluMeV5nTYaURsCA&_nc_ss=70689&_nc_map=urlgen_bucketless&_nc_zt=28&oh=00_AQQfWJqgA4VGCir2kfgQIbVLjyi0bAHpZKwJ7SslMNZfWA&oe=6AF413B6", "manifest_stream_number": 0, "is_dash_periods": true, "protocol": "https", "audio_ext": "m4a", "video_ext": "none", "vbr": 0, "abr": 53.851, "resolution": "audio only", "http_headers": {"User-Agent": "Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/149.0.0.0 Safari/537.36", "Accept": "text/html,application/xhtml+xml,application/xml;q=0.9,*/*;q=0.8", "Accept-Language": "en-us,en;q=0.5", "Sec-Fetch-Mode": "navigate", "Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "format": "dash-1483891280220710a - audio only (DASH audio)"}, {"url": "https://instagram.fblr2-3.fna.fbcdn.net/o1/v/t2/f2/m86/AQPjTqq_3H4X2_kD4dh-dz-xcaB96sR-pAYIXB4Dpa-BPlUrzjzz0yTmVGQvtb-55BgZSzX7Hpq7MBgbUfmQ7F30V2D2hFzjXRiVcxI.mp4?_nc_cat=108&_nc_oc=AdqJbM3F5O2PJq-ybRGsEbsj44YotfgRgivwfyQYSnbbOVEZoAWdrWoFCX69_TaUs-jlMn782N5mH70uk7RNJQjV&_nc_sid=5e9851&_nc_ht=instagram.fblr2-3.fna.fbcdn.net&_nc_ohc=9CUv2CU-iEIQ7kNvwHK5hYS&efg=eyJ2ZW5jb2RlX3RhZyI6Inhwdl9wcm9ncmVzc